==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|humidite|}}, from {{der|en|fro|humidité}}, from {{der|en|ML.|humiditas}}, from {{der|en|la|umidus||damp, moist, wet}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|humid|ity|nocat=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hjuːˈmɪd.ə.ti/|/hjuːˈmɪd.ɪ.ti/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-humidity.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/hjuˈmɪd.ə.ti/|[hjuˈmɪɾ.ə.ti]|[hjuˈmɪɾ.ə.ɾi]|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/hjʉːˈmɪd.ə.ti/|[hjuːˈmɪɾ.ə.ti]|[hjuːˈmɪɾ.ə.ɾi]|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪdəti|s=4}}
* {{hyph|en|hu|mi|di|ty}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# [[dampness|Dampness]], especially that of the [[air]].
# The [[amount]] of [[water]] [[vapour]] in the air.

